        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "52b8ff56-d0a3-3671-893e-7b029b30e02b",
                "word": "probité",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8ce9d5ce-1595-44cf-9233-c3d6325091b5",
                        "entry_id": "52b8ff56-d0a3-3671-893e-7b029b30e02b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "probités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "48bc02eb-3fe0-3af9-9b3a-1e722d2518ad",
                        "entry_id": "52b8ff56-d0a3-3671-893e-7b029b30e02b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualité d’une personne probe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3c4892e-2c0f-41ee-9ffa-8bc6627f41eb",
                                "sense_id": "48bc02eb-3fe0-3af9-9b3a-1e722d2518ad",
                                "text": "Je vais lui proposer d'être ici notre régisseur. Je crois qu'il nous secondera avec probité, expérience."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a8afe33-e1fc-4ca1-b86b-d5e84797cd56",
                                "sense_id": "48bc02eb-3fe0-3af9-9b3a-1e722d2518ad",
                                "text": "Quant à Latournelle, figurez-vous un bon petit homme, aussi rusé que la probité la plus pure le permet, et que tout étranger prendrait pour un fripon à voir l’étrange physionomie à laquelle le Havre s’est habitué."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cec3fc80-05ac-42c0-ad43-c35ddb9a4680",
                                "sense_id": "48bc02eb-3fe0-3af9-9b3a-1e722d2518ad",
                                "text": "La probité, c’est le trésor des pauvres gens, il faut bien posséder quelque chose !"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fd350a64-fd66-3cbe-a402-eb571bbad7aa",
                        "entry_id": "52b8ff56-d0a3-3671-893e-7b029b30e02b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Droiture, bonne foi, honnêteté rigoureuse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "843585e3-ba80-41d8-a1ea-23de259b5fe9",
                                "sense_id": "fd350a64-fd66-3cbe-a402-eb571bbad7aa",
                                "text": "Arrière l'honnêteté ! fi de la probité ! vautrons-nous dans toutes les jouissances d'abord…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "01cff409-a2bb-40f2-9dae-da57ef91e622",
                                "sense_id": "fd350a64-fd66-3cbe-a402-eb571bbad7aa",
                                "text": "Vêtu de probité candide et de lin blanc."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b7548df-2d91-430e-bebd-2fed17e16ae8",
                                "sense_id": "fd350a64-fd66-3cbe-a402-eb571bbad7aa",
                                "text": "Las, dans le petit monde de l'Université, la probité candide ne mène à rien, et l'enthousiasme pèse peu face aux manœuvres misérables de ceux qui ne reculent devant rien pour faire carrière."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dd059cef-3f8a-3930-94d2-d4fa2a476a9b",
                        "entry_id": "52b8ff56-d0a3-3671-893e-7b029b30e02b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Observation scrupuleuse des règles de la morale sociale, des devoirs imposés par la justice."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b01b604-3f93-47d8-83d8-5d76e07cbc47",
                                "sense_id": "dd059cef-3f8a-3930-94d2-d4fa2a476a9b",
                                "text": "M. Fabre représentait l'Honneur, la Loyauté, la Probité, la vie régulière et laborieuse, le livret de Caisse d’Épargne, le pain gagné à la sueur d'un front d'exploité, — bref tout ce que les bourgeois proclament des lèvres comme des vertus civiques."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0337b34-afd3-41d6-942b-c03d7bb123f6",
                                "sense_id": "dd059cef-3f8a-3930-94d2-d4fa2a476a9b",
                                "text": "Le commissaire aux comptes exerce sa profession avec honnêteté et droiture. Il s'abstient, en toutes circonstances, de tout agissement contraire à l'honneur et à la probité."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "41b84cb9-0f91-4d0f-a71e-e79ff743d468",
                                "sense_id": "dd059cef-3f8a-3930-94d2-d4fa2a476a9b",
                                "text": "Qu'est-ce que la vertu ? Au sens où l'entend son restaurateur, c'est sans doute la probité et le désintéressement, c'est ce genre d’intégrité qui rend un fonctionnaire ou un mandataire inaccessible à toutes les tentations, à toutes les corruptions […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "134da7d7-0436-407c-97d2-e81679224b13",
                        "source_entry_id": "52b8ff56-d0a3-3671-893e-7b029b30e02b",
                        "target_lang_word": "Redlichkeit",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Redlichkeit",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03643c00-1001-3761-8420-eacfa4b218b9",
                                        "entry_id": "234df5e3-d610-3749-a126-293bd700a8ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Eigenschaft einer Person, normgerecht und pflichtbewusst zu handeln"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f816966-16ba-461c-b977-7a2551f80da0",
                                                "sense_id": "03643c00-1001-3761-8420-eacfa4b218b9",
                                                "text": "Haben sie immer Redlichkeit geübt?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "973649a6-e387-421b-a5bf-bd903aab1434",
                                                "sense_id": "03643c00-1001-3761-8420-eacfa4b218b9",
                                                "text": "„Im Übrigen war er, besonders in den frühen, ab 1936 erscheinenden Bänden seines Werkes, ein großer, um Redlichkeit bemühter Porträtist nicht nur seiner Helden, sondern auch der Gegner seiner Helden.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0176625c-d215-4648-90ce-f63f3d0d9bb7",
                                                "sense_id": "03643c00-1001-3761-8420-eacfa4b218b9",
                                                "text": "„Die ausgeprägte Form von Nase, Mund und Kinn, das Ebenmaß seines Körpers, alles deutete auf eine Redlichkeit, die nicht versiegen würde.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d6d5c403-1403-4da2-abf3-0c9eff04d11c",
                        "source_entry_id": "52b8ff56-d0a3-3671-893e-7b029b30e02b",
                        "target_lang_word": "probity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "probity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e207721c-f779-32d4-9d65-293174ce5bce",
                                        "entry_id": "69fc911c-570e-3200-9cc9-da8e8a9ef69e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Integrity, especially of the quality of having strong moral principles; decency and honesty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a1ded67-d52b-4328-81d0-ead60af68e34",
                                                "sense_id": "e207721c-f779-32d4-9d65-293174ce5bce",
                                                "text": "[…] they can but bend our hearts to the love of probity and true honour […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac22aa0e-4b58-452b-9c8f-01fd9f9bde07",
                                                "sense_id": "e207721c-f779-32d4-9d65-293174ce5bce",
                                                "text": "[W]hen the interests or reputation of their own nation come into collision with those of another, they go to the opposite extreme, and forget their usual probity and candour, in the indulgence of spleen, and an illiberal spirit of ridicule."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3c4d4d2-36ca-4531-8ae2-561a6ea29e14",
                                                "sense_id": "e207721c-f779-32d4-9d65-293174ce5bce",
                                                "text": "Distilled to its essence, it is by no means clear that the ‘Cablegate’ disclosures were intended to support freedom of information, transparency, probity in government, or defence of the public interest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "061f1c46-79b8-4abe-b16e-414478b075e4",
                                                "sense_id": "e207721c-f779-32d4-9d65-293174ce5bce",
                                                "text": "The veterans add in their letter, which was partly coordinated by the campaign group Republic: “Officers of the British armed forces must adhere to the very highest standards of probity, honesty and honourable conduct. […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "01c0ad99-84be-4c75-9e85-6ef4b66aed6a",
                        "source_entry_id": "52b8ff56-d0a3-3671-893e-7b029b30e02b",
                        "target_lang_word": "honesty",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "honesty",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e80cd6b9-7701-3879-8300-c71dcca0f7b5",
                                        "entry_id": "36d6c2c4-3fd8-33bc-9ad0-042dffe99026",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act, quality, or condition of being honest."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4624d23-fd06-4138-a1ed-2b4235cd29bd",
                                                "sense_id": "e80cd6b9-7701-3879-8300-c71dcca0f7b5",
                                                "text": "academic / artistic / emotional / intellectual honesty"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28a4c0d2-e815-4417-98bd-d99cd49c90a1",
                                                "sense_id": "e80cd6b9-7701-3879-8300-c71dcca0f7b5",
                                                "text": "brutal / devastating / searing honesty"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da12768b-a5e1-49c3-9a8f-780441a2eae0",
                                                "sense_id": "e80cd6b9-7701-3879-8300-c71dcca0f7b5",
                                                "text": "There’s no trust, / No faith, no honesty in men; all perjured, / All forsworn, all naught, all dissemblers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e75e1cb-2086-4789-baa9-c802ae305533",
                                                "sense_id": "e80cd6b9-7701-3879-8300-c71dcca0f7b5",
                                                "text": "1787, George Colman, Junior, Inkle and Yarico, London: G.G.J. & J. Robinson, Act 2, p. 45,\nO give me your plain dealing Fellows\nWho never from honesty shrink;\nNot thinking on all they shou’d tell us,\nBut telling us all that they think."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92a4bd1c-8abf-4ced-b7f9-f27347896b62",
                                                "sense_id": "e80cd6b9-7701-3879-8300-c71dcca0f7b5",
                                                "text": "[…] Are you honest, boy? / Then be not spendthrift of your honesty, / But keep it to yourself; in Padua / Men think that honesty is ostentatious, so / It is not of the fashion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2aa4285a-cb24-4c72-a4c8-3f74a6d24289",
                                                "sense_id": "e80cd6b9-7701-3879-8300-c71dcca0f7b5",
                                                "text": "To those who knew her and to the greatly enlarged circle who were electrified by her last poems and sudden death, she had come to signify the specific honesties and risks of the poet’s condition."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54867009-155e-3a51-b913-bc7b2af10a8e",
                                        "entry_id": "36d6c2c4-3fd8-33bc-9ad0-042dffe99026",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Honor; decency, propriety."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02012f49-789c-40fc-ba29-63f2420e14ec",
                                                "sense_id": "54867009-155e-3a51-b913-bc7b2af10a8e",
                                                "text": "Have ye no wit, manners, nor honesty, but to gabble like tinkers at this time of night?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc6092e2-0f95-4858-8843-ff0301c35d90",
                                                "sense_id": "54867009-155e-3a51-b913-bc7b2af10a8e",
                                                "text": "Fellovves in armes faithfull and valiant, / I thanke you for your paines and honeſties, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49ba45f2-5759-45ea-9e80-dbb5c1a7444a",
                                                "sense_id": "54867009-155e-3a51-b913-bc7b2af10a8e",
                                                "text": "[…] that we may lead a quiet and peaceable life in all godliness and honesty."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f5a23389-9d2f-355b-8058-3c90f96cdb72",
                                        "entry_id": "36d6c2c4-3fd8-33bc-9ad0-042dffe99026",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chastity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8045188-c6bf-4549-935e-2749d4b8e2f7",
                                                "sense_id": "f5a23389-9d2f-355b-8058-3c90f96cdb72",
                                                "text": "[…] spend all I have; only give me so much of your time in exchange of it, as to lay an amiable siege to the honesty of this Ford’s wife […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29be6351-5bf4-470c-8105-a647778c1529",
                                                "sense_id": "f5a23389-9d2f-355b-8058-3c90f96cdb72",
                                                "text": "c. 1625, John Fletcher, The Fair Maid of the Inn, Act V, Scene 1, in Alexander Dyce (editor), The Works of Beaumont and Fletcher, New York: Appleton, 1890, Volume 2, p. 669,\n[…] Oh, these vild women,\nThat are so ill preservers of men’s honours,\nThey cannot govern their own honesties!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f0b303d-a491-3a70-bcc5-67f73ed9518b",
                                        "entry_id": "36d6c2c4-3fd8-33bc-9ad0-042dffe99026",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various crucifers in the genus Lunaria, several of which are grown as ornamentals, particularly annual honesty (Lunaria annua)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89822d94-5d5a-4824-8f57-123216c31c54",
                                                "sense_id": "4f0b303d-a491-3a70-bcc5-67f73ed9518b",
                                                "text": "Various measures were taken to avoid it, most popular being the suspension of certain herbs and tree branches over the doorways of dwellings and stables. Commonly used greenery were tansy, honesty, garlic, St. John's Wort, mountain ash, roadside verbena."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d135cff8-2a6f-438a-aa8b-ed5f8ab09c62",
                                                "sense_id": "4f0b303d-a491-3a70-bcc5-67f73ed9518b",
                                                "text": "She thought a minute, then stepped nimbly back into her cottage; and what she came out with at last was, a sprig of dry leaves, round as shillings, white as paper, quivering on a few thin stalks that looked ready to snap. / It was honesty."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
